        <mxCell id="JIhAfnByFY173I8j4Z0U-8" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Comic Sans MS;strokeColor=#808080;strokeWidth=0.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;" value="* to process and store information about the tree. It uses an Euler tour to represent the tree&lt;br&gt;*&amp;nbsp;by traversing the vertices in the order of an Euler tour, recording the appearance order, along with the entry and exit times of each vertex (in[], out[]). This helps map tree problems into array problems, using data structures like Sparse Table or Segment Tree to optimize queries.&lt;div&gt;*&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(255, 230, 204);&quot;&gt;The main application of an Euler tour is to flatten a tree.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
